  "step_1": "The decision reason compares the outcomes of the two lotteries, specifically focusing on the maximum and minimum outcomes. Lottery A has a single outcome of 2400 Euros with 100% probability, so its maximum and minimum outcome are both 2400 Euros. Lottery B has outcomes of 2500 Euros (33%), 2400 Euros (66%), and 0 Euros (1%). Thus, the maximum outcome of B is 2500 Euros, and the minimum is 0 Euros. The reason prefers the lottery with the more favorable maximum outcome; if those are equal, it then compares the minimum outcomes. Here, B has a higher maximum outcome (2500 > 2400), so according to the reason, B should be preferred. The relevant information for the reason is therefore clearly present and derivable from the lotteries' structure.",
